Well, the one YANI I mentioned that people seemed to like was
cockatrice scale armor.

Basically the idea was to have a similar situation as DSM but with
cockatrices, and it gives you stoning resistance. Originally the idea
was for armor, like the dragon scales, but cockatrices are supposed to
be small, so that doesn't make much sense. So, either boots or helmet.
Let's assume boots for now (to compete with speed boots). I'll explain
my final idea and later explain the rationales.

Cockatrice scales are dropped when killing cockatrices at a rate
similar to dragon scales. Non-blessed cockatrice scales stone you
instantly just like a corpse (but only the holder, can't be used as
weapon). Blessed cockatrice scales start a slow stoning process.
Handling them with gloves is ok, as normal. Wearing them (as boots)
stone you as handling them without gloves, of course.

Cockatrice scale mail boots (or some other name) are created by
reading an enchant armor scroll while wearing cockatrice scales. They
stop any stoning process and give you stoning resistance. If they ever
become cursed, you get stoned (or should I say petrified?).


Note that wearing cockatrice scale mail armor allows you to go around
with a rubber chicken with impunity, only worrying about them becoming
cursed. You can also have a bunch of cockatrice pets and even use
conflict with them. Fortunately you can't ride cockatrices, as that
would be overpowered.


Discarded ideas:
-Can't make cockatrice scale armor stone both you and everything that
touches you. That's too powerful because gargoyles can wear armor.
(Yes you can polymorph into a cockatrice, but then you can't carry
much at all). It would also make fighting Demogorgon too easy (put
blessed ones on, Demo dies, take them off and drink acid).
-Blessed cockatrice scales only stone you slowly so that you can put
them on and have time to read a scroll of enchant armor  (which stops
the stoning).
-This would be better if it took up the armor slot, to compete with
?DSM, but as mentioned cockatrices are small.
-Technically it makes more sense to put them on your head, as a helmet
is easier to make than boots, but then it would be an easier choice,
even with the curse insta-death.
-Do disenchanters turn DSM into dragon scales? That might be applied
to cockatrice scales too with good results.

I took a quick look at what it would take to implement it, and it
doesn't look too bad. I don't have time to do it anytime soon though.
I'll do it in a couple months if nobody beats me to it.



